  "details": "1. Create an Udon program and add/use the SetAvatarEyeHeightMinimumByMeters method in order to set the minimum height to something greater than 0.2.\n\n2. Add the SetAvatarEyeHeightMaximumByMeters method in order to set the maximum height to something lower than the minimum height.\n\nThe behaviour doesn't entirely break when setting the maximum height below the minimum height, but the Avatar Height slider works unexpectedly. What I as a user expected from this was that it would lower the minimum height to the same value as the maximum height when the maximum height is set to be lower.",
